,"7":6,"8":7,"9":8,"10":9,"11":10,"12":11,"13":12,"14":13,"15":13,"16":14,"17":15,"18":18,"19":19,"20":20,"21":21,"22":22,"23":23,"24":24,"25":25,"26":26,"27":27,"28":28,"29":29,"30":29,"31":30,"32":32,"33":32,"34":34,"35":36,"36":37,"37":38,"38":39,"39":40,"40":41,"41":42,"42":43,"43":44,"44":45,"45":46,"46":47,"47":47,"48":49,"49":49,"50":51,"51":51,"52":53,"53":54},"notes":{"ts":{"2":"<code>a</code> is the heap as an array: every parent is at least as large as its children.","3":"How many job kinds are ready to run.","6":"Work on the heap array directly.","7":"Add the new count at the end.","8":"<code>i</code> is the new count's position.","9":"Move it up while it is not at the root.","10":"Index of its parent.","11":"The parent is already at least as large, so the heap order holds.","12":"Swap the larger count up.","13":"Continue from the parent's position.","18":"Keep the root to return, and remove the last element.","19":"If anything is left, the empty root needs filling.","20":"Move the last element into the root.","21":"Start sinking it from the root.","22":"Sink until it is at least as large as both children.","23":"Indexes of the two children.","24":"<code>m</code> will be the largest of the node and its children.","25":"The left child is larger so far.","26":"The right child is larger still.","27":"The node is the largest, so the heap order holds.","28":"Swap the larger child up.","29":"Continue from the child's position.","32":"Return the removed largest count.","37":"<code>count</code> maps each job kind to how many jobs of it remain.","38":"Tally the jobs of each kind.","39":"The heap holds the remaining counts of kinds that are ready to run.","40":"Every kind starts out ready.","41":"<code>wait</code> queues kinds cooling down, in the order their cooldowns end.","42":"<code>head</code> is the first kind still waiting; <code>time</code> is the current slot.","43":"Continue while some kind is ready or still cooling down.","44":"Move to the next slot.","